{"attempt_id": "attempt:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-source-fidelity-01", "created_at": "2026-09-06T08:00:00Z", "graph_id": "graph:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-v1", "obligations": [{"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof", "counterexample", "formalization", "computation"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": ["obligation:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-statement-fidelity"], "kind": "root_claim", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-root", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-2359"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "We let $Q_d$ denote the $d$-dimensional cube graph. A map $\\phi: E(Q_d) \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}$ is called edge-antipodal if $\\phi(e) \\neq \\phi(e')$ whenever $e,e'$ are antipodal edges. Conjecture If $d \\ge 2$ and $\\phi: E(Q_d) \\rightarrow \\{0,1\\}$ is edge-antipodal, then there exist a pair of antipodal vertices $v,v' \\in V(Q_d)$ which are joined by a monochromatic path."}, "statement_sha256": "74ae52fb9924f8da0027400f49e15c5efd1742bbd55d3c800a1e67481869f6c7"}, {"acceptance": {"allowed_candidate_kinds": ["proof"], "required_capabilities": ["human_review", "statement_faithfulness"]}, "dependencies": [], "kind": "definition", "obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-statement-fidelity", "source_refs": ["https://www.unsolvedmath.com/problems/OPG-2359"], "statement": {"formal_declaration": null, "language": "en", "text": "Verify against the cited source that the frozen statement is complete, current, untruncated, attribution-correct, and unambiguous enough for mathematical research; record any definition or quantifier gap without silently editing the contract."}, "statement_sha256": "65f0b3d574bd6d837403149dab6434c0f571709f7eb5bb066c7e8774bad13f34"}], "problem_contract_sha256": "2574b66ee7e9f1d6ec8311ffdd17ff844e2091766133d33203bf458e6bfbcb19", "problem_id": "problem:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9", "root_obligation_id": "obligation:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-root", "route_id": "route:um-opg-2359-edge-antipodal-colorings-of-cubes-b14941c9-source-fidelity", "schema_version": "1.0.0", "supersedes": null}
